    STEP A-3.19: Direct Internal Test Hooks & TSan Concurrency Coverage
    
    Resolves the critical TSan coverage gap from A-3.18 audit:
    T8/T9/T10 were being SKIPPED under TSan because they used free()/realloc()
    which go through the profiler's interposition wrappers (disabled under
    sanitizer). This meant the mutex-protected registry code was never
    exercised under race detection.
    
    FIX: Added DIRECT test hooks that call internal profiler functions
    WITHOUT going through the malloc/realloc/free interposition wrappers:
    
      __profiler_v6_test_bootstrap_free()      — calls bootstrap_deregister directly
      __profiler_v6_test_bootstrap_realloc()  — exercises full bootstrap realloc path
      __profiler_v6_test_direct_track_alloc() — calls track_alloc directly
      __profiler_v6_test_direct_track_free()  — calls track_free directly
      __profiler_v6_test_is_tracked()        — checks g_ptr_table membership
    
    These hooks work under TSan even when g_profiler_disabled is set, because
    they don't check that flag — they call the internal static functions
    directly. TSan instruments these functions (compiled with -fsanitize=thread),
    so every mutex lock/unlock, every memory access in bootstrap_deregister/
    lookup/alloc/realloc IS visible to the race detector.
    
    T8/T9/T10 rewritten to use direct hooks instead of free()/realloc():
      T8: uses __profiler_v6_test_bootstrap_free instead of free()
      T9: uses __profiler_v6_test_bootstrap_free for writer cleanup
      T10: REWRITTEN to use __profiler_v6_test_bootstrap_realloc for all
           bootstrap realloc tests (grow, shrink, realloc(,0), failure injection)
    
    SKIP_IF_DISABLED removed from T8/T9/T10 — they now run unconditionally.
    
    Results:
      Plain suite: 89 tests, exit 0
      TSan: exit 0, 0 data races, 0 warnings, 0 size aborts
      T8 under TSan: 6 tests RAN (not skipped) — concurrency/ABA/slot reuse
      T9 under TSan: 6 tests RAN (not skipped) — concurrent lookup/deregister
      T10 under TSan: 19 tests RAN (not skipped) — bootstrap realloc + failure
      Node smoke: exit 0
      PROD isolation: verified (nm -D, zero test-hook symbols)
    
    Script now explicitly checks: T8/T9/T10 skipped count must be 0.
    
    No push to feature branch (awaiting Steward approval).

